    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d257">

                <pb facs="0407" n="395" sameAs="frus:frus1945v06/pg395"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.94114A/8–2045: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Harrison</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-08-20">August 20,
                        1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2565. Request Swiss Foreign Office to ask Swiss representatives in Jap and former
                    Jap occupied territories to give full cooperation to Allied military authorities
                    who have plans for evacuation of POWs and CIs.<anchor n="29" xml:id="d257-f1"/>
                    POWs and CIs should remain in camps in close contact with camp spokesmen until
                    arrival of Allied forces.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d257-f1" n="29" xml:id="d257-f1-content">
                <p>In telegram 2628, August 28, 7 p.m., to Bern, the Department stated: “Mil
                    authorities in Pacific have plan for orderly evacuation from camps to specified
                    ports and then to Manila where final processing will take place and repatriation
                    will be effected immediately after the surrender terms are signed.”
                    (711.94114A/8–2345)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
